WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.120
It turns out that becoming an instant icon
isn't always the greatest thing for a child's

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.620
psyche.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.900
Emma Watson, who was cast as Hermione Granger
in the Harry Potter film series at the tender

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.459
age of nine, recently opened up to British
Vogue about her years-long struggle with guilt

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.120
over having landed the plum role.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.540
Watson was famously plucked from a crowd of
would-be Hermiones during open auditions at

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.170
her school, and as soon as Potter fans were
introduced to her in 2001's Harry Potter and

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.160
the Sorcerer's Stone - or Philosopher’s
Stone in the UK, they knew that the role had

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.260
been perfectly cast.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.380
Her droll delivery and adult mannerisms suited
Hermione perfectly, and as the series' cast

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.320
grew into young adults over the course of
eight films, it became clear that Watson's

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.440
formidable talent was growing as well.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.560
"Boys, I think it's time we teach Weasely
how to respect his superiors."

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.640
"Hope you don't mean yourself."

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.240
But immediate worldwide fame can obviously
be tough for any kid to handle, and Watson

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.180
was no different.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.410
In her conversation with Vogue, the actress
said that she experienced a great deal of

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.820
guilt over feeling burdened by said fame when
the role could have gone to any number of

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.120
other young actresses perhaps one who would
have handled the exposure better.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:05.880
The star said:

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.300
"I've sat in therapy and felt really guilty
about, to be honest."

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.740
"Like, why me?

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.479
Somebody else would have enjoyed and wanted
it more than I did."

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:21.312
The actress went on to say that, as a child,
it was truly impossible to know exactly what

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.680
she was signing up for when producers picked
her to play Hermione.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:30.780
"I was nine years old, and I got literally
picked out of a lineup in my school gym.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.480
It wasn't even an acting school."

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.500
The star related how, as Pottermania swept
the globe, she had to make a conscious effort

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.220
to reorient herself mentally in the face of
massive worldwide fame.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.220
Watson explained:

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.840
"And part of, I think, my sense of peace within
myself has been in remembering my identity."

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.780
"I belong to a family, I come from a place,
I have roots.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.360
There's a whole really big existence and identity
that I have"

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.380
Watson's is a struggle that has been faced
by child actors for generations, but even

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:03.290
among their ranks, a few have experienced
being part of a global phenomenon like Harry

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:03.860
Potter.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.360
Adapted from the wildly popular young adult
novels by J.K.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:11.480
Rowling, the eight films in the main series
combined to gross nearly $8 billion dollars

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.780
at the worldwide box office.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.720
When the Fantastic Beasts spin-off films,
in which Watson did not appear, are factored

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.480
in, Harry Potter is the third-highest grossing
film franchise in history behind only the

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.860
juggernauts that are the Marvel Cinematic
Universe and Star Wars.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.060
On top of that, the main Potter cast literally
grew up in front of the camera playing the

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:33.220
same characters, a situation even fewer child
actors have had to contend with.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.280
It was a prolonged and intense level of attention
that would have been enough to make just about

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.160
any ordinary kid flame out.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.900
But thankfully, Watson and her co-stars Daniel
Radcliffe and Rupert Grint managed to come

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.790
away from the experience as well-adjusted,
successful adults.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.739
Watson in particular has continued working
steadily since the main Potter series ended,

00:02:51.739 --> 00:02:56.320
appearing in such films as The Bling Ring
and Noah before scoring another mega-hit with

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.721
Disney's 2017 live-action adaptation of Beauty
and the Beast, which took home well over a

00:03:01.721 --> 00:03:03.010
billion dollars globally.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.670
This Christmas Day, she can be seen in the
latest adaptation of Louisa May Alcott's classic

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.580
novel Little Women Despite stiff competition
from the likes of Jumanji: The Next Level

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.550
and Star Wars Episode IX: The Rise of Skywalker,
the flick is expected to do respectable box

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.440
office thanks to its blinding star power and
the sure guiding hand of writer/director Greta

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:27.820
Gerwig, the creative mind behind 2017's widely
acclaimed coming-of-age dramedy Lady Bird.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:32.120
Of course, Watson's present success largely
came at the cost of anything resembling a

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:36.240
normal childhood, but the actress seems to
have come to terms with her experience and

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.620
the struggles that came with it.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.819
Even if she had never made another film after
the Harry Potter series, she would have been

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:46.019
fondly remembered by fans around the world,
but her boatload of talent ensures that she'll

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:50.379
be gracing the silver screen for years to
come something she no longer feels quite so

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.379
bad about.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.160
"It took me a long time, but I'm very happy."

